# tests/guix-glibc-locpath.supp: the memory gate's one suppression
# (ADR-0014). make test-memory hands it to Valgrind only in a Guix environment
# (GUIX_ENVIRONMENT set). CI passes none.
#
# In the Guix container, loading libcurl runs p11-kit's constructor, which
# calls newlocale. Guix's glibc patch for GUIX_LOCPATH adds
# compute_locale_search_path, and it loses one block there every time: 171
# bytes with the container's GUIX_LOCPATH. Upstream glibc has no such
# function, and Ubuntu loses nothing. It is not chez-curl's leak.
#
# make check-memory-gate holds this file to exactly the entry below. It also
# requires a container run that loads libcurl to report the entry used on
# one block, the same run without it to fail on that block, and the planted
# leak to fail with it read. Widening it takes an amendment to ADR-0014.
{
   guix-glibc-locpath
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:realloc
   fun:argz_add_sep
   fun:compute_locale_search_path
   fun:newlocale
}
